[h1]Bug Reports[/h1]
Post bugs in this thread only. One bug per reply, so each can be tracked and answered. Questions and suggestions belong in their own threads.

[h2]Before you post[/h2]
[olist]
    [*]Make sure UE4SS Experimental (Palworld) is subscribed and enabled, and that Palpedia Enhancer is enabled under Options > Mod Management.
    [*]Restart Palworld once. Mods install on launch, not on subscribe.
    [*]Check whether the bug still happens with every other mod disabled. If it goes away, say which mod brings it back.
[/olist]

[h2]Turn on verbose logging[/h2]
Open [noparse]Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\1623730\3788253343\Assets\Settings.ini[/noparse] in Notepad, change the VerboseLogging line to:
[code]VerboseLogging=true[/code]
Restart Palworld, reproduce the bug, then close the game. Turn it back to false afterwards; it makes the log large.

[h2]What to include[/h2]
Copy this template into your reply and fill in every line:
[code]
Mod version:        (Options > Mod Management, or the first Palpedia Enhancer line in UE4SS.log)
Palworld version:   (bottom left of the title screen, for example v1.0.3.101283)
Where:              (singleplayer / co-op host / co-op client / dedicated server client)
Other mods:         (the full list, or "none")
Language:           (the game language you play in)
What I did:         (step by step, starting from opening the Palpedia)
What happened:
What I expected:
Log:                (link to the file, see below)
[/code]

[h2]The log[/h2]
The file is [noparse]Steam\steamapps\common\Palworld\Mods\NativeMods\UE4SS\UE4SS.log[/noparse]. It is overwritten every launch, so copy it right after the bug happens. Steam comments strip long pastes, so upload the whole file to a paste site or file host and link it. Do not paste only the lines you think matter: the cause is usually earlier than the symptom.

[h2]If the game crashed[/h2]
Also attach the newest folder from [noparse]%LocalAppData%\Pal\Saved\Crashes[/noparse]. The file [noparse]CrashContext.runtime-xml[/noparse] inside it names the exact line at fault. If that file does not mention [noparse]PalpediaEnhancer[/noparse] or [noparse]main.dll[/noparse], the crash is most likely from something else, but post it anyway and it will be checked.

[h2]What happens next[/h2]
Confirmed bugs are fixed in a PATCH update, listed in the Change Notes tab. A reply in this thread will say which version carries the fix. Reports missing the log or the version are answered with a request for them before anything else.

[h2]Not bugs[/h2]
[list]
    [*]"Palpedia Enhancer turned itself off" in UE4SS.log after a Palworld update: that is the mod protecting your game until it is updated for the new build. Watch the Change Notes.
    [*]Buttons in English while the game is in another language: a missing translation falls back to English on purpose. Post the language and the button in the Translations thread instead.
[/list]
